---
title: FrontierJS — coming soon
description: One schema file seeds your database, your API, and your UI. FrontierJS is coming soon — read the journey while it gets there.
render: static
---
<!--
  The splash. One screen that says what is coming and hands the reader to the
  journey; the long-form case is /pitch/. The only scripts are the layout's theme
  island and the landscape cloud below the splash, so the splash motion is CSS and
  stops under reduced-motion.
-->
<script>
  import Marquee from '@frontierjs/site-kit/blocks/Marquee.mesa'
  import LandscapeCloud from '../islands/LandscapeCloud.mesa'
  import { derived } from '../data/derived.js'

  export let data = null

  const d = data ?? { projects: [], factors: [], stances: [] }
  const first = d.projects[0] ?? null
</script>

<section id="top" class="splash">
  <div class="backdrop" aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="layer ground">
      <div class="map"></div>
      <div class="drift shadows"></div>
    </div>
    <div class="layer wisps"><div class="drift"></div></div>
    <div class="layer lows"><div class="drift"></div></div>
  </div>
  <div class="veil" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <div class="glow" aria-hidden="true"></div>

  <div class="container inner">
    <!-- <p class="eyebrow">
      <span class="badge warning">Coming soon</span>
      FrontierJS
    </p> -->

    <h1>The Frontier<br><span class="accent">is coming.</span></h1>

    <p class="lede">
      One starting source of truth. Get your database, API and UI
      …with validation, authorization, pagination, live updates, migrations, typed clients and forms
      <strong>derived, not written</strong>.
    </p>

    <div class="cluster ctas">
      <a class="btn text-xl raised glass" href="/journey/">Follow the journey →</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="why" aria-labelledby="why-title">
  <div class="container grid">
    <div class="case">
      <p class="eyebrow">Why</p>
      <h2 id="why-title">Why another framework?</h2>
      <p>
        Because most of a web app is restatement. A Lead has an email, so the schema
        says so. So do the validator, the TypeScript type, the access middleware and
        the API docs. That's five copies of one fact, and sooner or later two of them
        disagree.
      </p>
      <p>
        Most frameworks help you write that glue faster. FrontierJS derives it, so
        there is no second copy to drift.
      </p>
      <blockquote>Every duplicated truth eventually becomes a duplicated mental model.</blockquote>
    </div>

    <div class="reasons">
      <h3>Why this one</h3>
      <ol>
        <li>
          <b>One file is the origin.</b>
          <code>db/schema.lite</code> seeds the tables, migrations, API, typed client,
          forms and live updates. Each is a projection of it, never a second source.
        </li>
        <li>
          <b>The rules travel with the data.</b>
          Who can read, write or change a status is declared on the model with
          <code>@@gate</code>, <code>@guarded</code> and <code>@@transitions</code>, and
          enforced at the data. No route, job or agent gets around it.
        </li>
        <li>
          <b>Three nouns to learn.</b>
          Model, Service, Resource. Know those and you can guess where a feature lives
          before you read its docs.
        </li>
        <li>
          <b>Yours, not a platform.</b>
          Your app stays a file tree, a binary and a SQLite database you own and run.
        </li>
      </ol>
      <p class="more">
        <a class="link" href="/direction/story/">The long version →</a>
        <a class="link" href="/why/">When not to use it: pre-alpha, Bun and SQLite only →</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="landscape" aria-labelledby="landscape-title">
  <div class="container">
    <h2 id="landscape-title">Nothing here was invented</h2>
    <p class="lede">
      FrontierJS is assembled out of {d.projects.length} other projects. Each word is one of them,
      sized by <span data-factor-label>how close it is</span>; hover one to see what was
      taken and where it stops.
    </p>

    <div class="controls">
      <div class="segmented" data-factors role="group" aria-label="Size the cloud by">
        {#each d.factors as f}
          <button data-factor={f.key} data-label={f.label} data-help={f.help}
                  aria-pressed={f.key === 'closeness'}>{f.label}</button>
        {/each}
      </div>
      <div class="legend" aria-label="Tier">
        <span><i style="background:var(--tier-1)"></i> Direct lineage</span>
        <span><i style="background:var(--tier-2)"></i> Partial overlap</span>
        <span><i style="background:var(--tier-3)"></i> Ancestors</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Filled at mount: the cloud is packed against the box it is measured in. -->
    <div class="cloud" data-cloud data-state="static"></div>

    <div class="detail" data-detail>
      {#each d.projects as p}
        <div class="proj" class:is-shown={p.rank === first?.rank} data-rank={p.rank}>
          <div class="head">
            <span class="name">{p.name}</span>
            <span class="meta">{p.realm} · tier {p.tier} · closeness {p.closeness} · influence {p.inspiration}</span>
          </div>
          <p><span class="k">Taken</span>{p.relation}</p>
          <p><span class="k">Stops at</span>{p.gap}</p>
        </div>
      {/each}
    </div>

    <!-- The island reads each word off these, and reorders them. They are the
         crawlable list too, so they stay in the flow, clipped. -->
    <ul class="visually-hidden" data-rows>
      {#each d.projects as p}
        <li class="entry" data-rank={p.rank} data-name={p.name} data-url={p.url}
            data-tier={p.tier} data-stance={p.stance}
            data-closeness={p.closeness} data-inspiration={p.inspiration}
            data-proximity={p.proximity}>
          <a href={p.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener">{p.name}</a> — {p.relation}
        </li>
      {/each}
    </ul>

    <p class="more"><a class="link" href="/why/landscape/">The full register — what was taken, where it stops, what we did with it →</a></p>
  </div>
</section>

<LandscapeCloud client:load />

<section class="derived" aria-labelledby="derived-title">
  <h2 id="derived-title" class="container">Derived from the schema, extended by you</h2>
  <Marquee label="Everything the schema derives" duration="860s" gap="1rem">
    {#each derived as d}
      <article class="feature">
        <h3>{d.title}</h3>
        <p>{d.line}</p>
        {#if d.tag}<code>{d.tag}</code>{/if}
      </article>
    {/each}
  </Marquee>
</section>

<style>
  .splash {
    position: relative; overflow: hidden; isolation: isolate;
    min-height: calc(100svh - var(--sticky-offset, 4rem));
    display: grid; align-items: center;
    padding: 4rem 0 5rem;
    font-family: var(--font-primary);
  }

  /* The territory map, toured: six stops and back to the first, so the loop
     has no seam. A stop is a zoom and the point it zooms toward, as a share of
     the box; zooming toward a point inside the box never uncovers an edge,
     which a translate past the scaled overhang would.

     Three cloud tiles ride the same tour. The shadows lie on the ground and
     scale with the map; the wisps and the low clouds scale by --depth times as
     much toward the same point, so on a dive they open past the camera faster
     than the land below them. Each tile also drifts on its own clock, and
     wraps, so the drift has no seam either.
     /splash-tune/ edits all of this live and prints the block back to paste. */
  .backdrop {
    position: absolute; inset: 0; z-index: -3;
    container-type: size;
    --tour-length: 180s;
    --tour-easing: ease-in-out;
    --stop0-zoom: 1.9;   --stop0-x: 72%; --stop0-y: 42%;
    --stop1-zoom: 2.3;   --stop1-x: 88%; --stop1-y: 24%;
    --stop2-zoom: 1.15;  --stop2-x: 60%; --stop2-y: 50%;
    --stop3-zoom: 2.0;   --stop3-x: 74%; --stop3-y: 74%;
    --stop4-zoom: 1.7;   --stop4-x: 94%; --stop4-y: 86%;
    --stop5-zoom: 1.0;   --stop5-x: 50%; --stop5-y: 50%;
    --shadow-opacity: .8;  --shadow-drift: 300s;
    --wisp-opacity: .7;    --wisp-drift: 200s;   --wisp-depth: 1.25;
    --low-opacity: .9;     --low-drift: 140s;    --low-depth: 1.4;
  }
  .layer {
    position: absolute; inset: 0;
    will-change: transform, transform-origin;
    animation: tour var(--tour-length) var(--tour-easing) infinite;
  }
  .ground { --depth: 1; }
  .wisps  { --depth: var(--wisp-depth); opacity: var(--wisp-opacity); }
  .lows   { --depth: var(--low-depth);  opacity: var(--low-opacity); }

  .map {
    position: absolute; inset: 0;
    background: url('/map/territory.webp') 70% 40% / cover no-repeat;
    filter: saturate(.9);
  }

  /* One tile is at least as tall as the box, so it repeats only sideways, and
     a drift of exactly one tile width lands where it started. */
  .drift {
    --tile: max(100cqw, 160cqh);
    position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; height: 100%;
    width: calc(100% + var(--tile));
    background: var(--sprites) 0 50% / var(--tile) auto repeat-x;
    will-change: transform;
    animation: wind var(--drift) linear infinite;
  }
  .shadows {
    --sprites: url('/map/clouds-shadow.webp'); --drift: var(--shadow-drift);
    opacity: var(--shadow-opacity); mix-blend-mode: multiply;
  }
  .wisps .drift { --sprites: url('/map/clouds-wisp.webp'); --drift: var(--wisp-drift); }
  .lows .drift  { --sprites: url('/map/clouds-low.webp');  --drift: var(--low-drift); }

  @keyframes tour {
    0%, 100% { transform: scale(calc(1 + (var(--stop0-zoom) - 1) * var(--depth))); transform-origin: var(--stop0-x) var(--stop0-y); }
    16.667%  { transform: scale(calc(1 + (var(--stop1-zoom) - 1) * var(--depth))); transform-origin: var(--stop1-x) var(--stop1-y); }
    33.333%  { transform: scale(calc(1 + (var(--stop2-zoom) - 1) * var(--depth))); transform-origin: var(--stop2-x) var(--stop2-y); }
    50%      { transform: scale(calc(1 + (var(--stop3-zoom) - 1) * var(--depth))); transform-origin: var(--stop3-x) var(--stop3-y); }
    66.667%  { transform: scale(calc(1 + (var(--stop4-zoom) - 1) * var(--depth))); transform-origin: var(--stop4-x) var(--stop4-y); }
    83.333%  { transform: scale(calc(1 + (var(--stop5-zoom) - 1) * var(--depth))); transform-origin: var(--stop5-x) var(--stop5-y); }
  }
  @keyframes wind {
    to { transform: translateX(calc(-1 * var(--tile))); }
  }

  /* Mixed from --surface rather than a fixed white, so a dark theme dims the
     map instead of washing it out; the copy sits on the solid side. */
  .veil {
    position: absolute; inset: 0; z-index: -2;
    background:
      linear-gradient(to bottom, transparent 55%, var(--surface) 98%),
      linear-gradient(100deg,
        var(--surface) 0%,
        color-mix(in srgb, var(--surface) 88%, transparent) 38%,
        color-mix(in srgb, var(--surface) 55%, transparent) 70%,
        color-mix(in srgb, var(--surface) 35%, transparent) 100%);
  }
  @media (max-width: 48rem) {
    .veil {
      background:
        linear-gradient(to bottom, transparent 55%, var(--surface) 98%),
        color-mix(in srgb, var(--surface) 84%, transparent);
    }
  }

  /* Tinted from the theme's own primary, so every swatch in the topbar
     retints the splash rather than leaving a fixed color behind. */
  .glow {
    position: absolute; inset: -20% -10% auto auto; z-index: -1;
    width: min(60rem, 120vw); aspect-ratio: 1; border-radius: 50%;
    background: radial-gradient(closest-side,
      color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-primary) 28%, transparent),
      transparent 70%);
    filter: blur(20px);
    animation: drift 14s ease-in-out infinite alternate;
  }
  @keyframes drift {
    from { transform: translate(0, 0) scale(1); }
    to   { transform: translate(-12%, 18%) scale(1.15); }
  }

  .inner { display: grid; gap: 1.5rem; justify-items: start; padding-inline: 1.25rem; }

  .eyebrow {
    display: flex; align-items: center; gap: .75rem; margin: 0;
    font-size: .78rem; letter-spacing: .12em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--ink-mute);
  }
  .eyebrow .badge { letter-spacing: .06em; }

  h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2.75rem, 10vw, 6rem); line-height: .98; letter-spacing: -.04em;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .accent { color: var(--color-primary); }

  .lede { font-size: clamp(1.05rem, 2.2vw, 1.3rem); color: var(--ink-soft); max-width: 44ch; margin: 0; }

  .realms {
    list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: .5rem 0 0;
    display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; gap: .6rem;
  }
  .realms li:not(.arrow) {
    display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: .1rem;
    padding: .55rem .95rem; border-radius: var(--radius, 10px);
    border: 1px solid var(--rule-strong); background: var(--surface-raised);
    animation: rise .6s ease-out both;
  }
  .realms li:nth-child(3) { animation-delay: .15s; }
  .realms li:nth-child(5) { animation-delay: .3s; }
  .realms b { font-size: 1rem; }
  .realms span { font-size: .75rem; color: var(--ink-mute); }
  .realms .arrow { color: var(--ink-mute); }
  @keyframes rise {
    from { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(.5rem); }
    to   { opacity: 1; transform: none; }
  }

  .ctas { gap: .75rem; margin-top: .75rem; }
  /* An untoned ghost takes --color-primary, which is below AA on --surface in
     two shipped themes; the neutral ink is legible in all six. */
  .btn.ghost { color: var(--ink); }

  .promises {
    list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 2rem 0 0;
    display: grid; gap: 1rem 2rem; width: 100%;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(15rem, 1fr));
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); padding-top: 1.5rem;
  }
  .promises li { font-size: .92rem; color: var(--ink-soft); }
  .promises b { color: var(--ink); display: block; margin-bottom: .2rem; }

  .why { padding: 4rem 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); font-family: var(--font-primary); }
  .why .grid {
    display: grid; gap: 2.5rem 4rem; padding-inline: 1.25rem;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 22rem), 1fr));
  }
  .why h2 { font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 3.4vw, 2.3rem); letter-spacing: -.03em; line-height: 1.1; margin: 0 0 .6em; }
  .why .case p { color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: 1.05rem; line-height: 1.6; max-width: 52ch; margin: 0 0 1em; }
  .why blockquote {
    margin: 1.5rem 0 0; padding-left: 1rem; border-left: 3px solid var(--color-primary);
    font-size: 1.15rem; line-height: 1.45; color: var(--ink); max-width: 40ch;
  }
  .why h3 {
    margin: 0 0 1rem; font-size: .78rem; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: .12em;
    text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--ink-mute);
  }
  .why ol { list-style: none; counter-reset: why; padding: 0; margin: 0; display: grid; gap: 1.1rem; }
  .why li {
    counter-increment: why; position: relative; padding-left: 2.25rem;
    font-size: .95rem; line-height: 1.55; color: var(--ink-soft);
  }
  .why li::before {
    content: counter(why, decimal-leading-zero); position: absolute; left: 0; top: .1rem;
    font-family: var(--font-mono, ui-monospace, Menlo, monospace); font-size: .78rem; color: var(--color-primary);
  }
  .why li b { display: block; color: var(--ink); font-size: 1.02rem; margin-bottom: .15rem; }
  .why li code { font-family: var(--font-mono, ui-monospace, Menlo, monospace); font-size: .85em; }
  .why .more { display: grid; gap: .4rem; margin: 1.5rem 0 0; font-size: .92rem; }

  .landscape { padding: 3.5rem 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); font-family: var(--font-primary); }
  .landscape h2 { font-size: clamp(1.4rem, 3vw, 1.9rem); letter-spacing: -.02em; margin: 0 0 .35em; }
  .landscape .lede { font-size: 1.05rem; color: var(--ink-soft); max-width: 60ch; line-height: 1.6; margin: 0; }
  .landscape .more { margin: 1.25rem 0 0; font-size: .92rem; }

  /* The ordinal tier ramp, the same three the landscape page validated. */
  :root {
    --tier-1: #104281;
    --tier-2: #256abf;
    --tier-3: #5598e7;
    --cloud-hover: color-mix(in srgb, var(--tier-1) 12%, transparent);
  }
  :global(.theme-dark) {
    --tier-1: #b7d3f6;
    --tier-2: #6da7ec;
    --tier-3: #3987e5;
  }

  .controls { display: flex; gap: 1.25rem; align-items: center; flex-wrap: wrap; margin: 1.5rem 0 1rem; }
  .segmented { display: inline-flex; border: 1px solid var(--rule-strong); border-radius: 8px; overflow: hidden; }
  .segmented button {
    appearance: none; border: 0; background: var(--surface); color: var(--ink-soft);
    font: inherit; font-size: .85rem; padding: .4rem .85rem; cursor: pointer;
  }
  .segmented button + button { border-left: 1px solid var(--rule); }
  .segmented button[aria-pressed="true"] { background: var(--surface-sunken); color: var(--ink); font-weight: 600; }
  .legend { display: flex; gap: 1rem; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-left: auto; font-size: .8rem; color: var(--ink-soft); }
  .legend span { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: .4rem; }
  .legend i { width: .8rem; height: .8rem; border-radius: 3px; display: inline-block; }

  .cloud {
    position: relative;
    height: clamp(22rem, 58vh, 34rem);
    border: 1px solid var(--rule); border-radius: 14px;
    background: var(--surface-raised); overflow: hidden;
  }
  /* The words are made by the island, so they carry no scope id. */
  .cloud :global(a) {
    position: absolute; white-space: nowrap; text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: -.02em; line-height: 1;
    padding: .12em .2em; border-radius: 6px;
    transition: background-color .12s ease, transform .12s ease;
  }
  .cloud :global(a:hover), .cloud :global(a:focus-visible) { background: var(--cloud-hover); transform: scale(1.04); }
  .cloud :global(a:focus-visible) { outline: 2px solid var(--ink); outline-offset: 1px; }

  .detail {
    margin-top: 1rem; border: 1px solid var(--rule); border-left: 4px solid var(--tier-1);
    border-radius: 10px; background: var(--surface-raised); padding: 1rem 1.15rem;
    min-height: 8.5rem;
  }
  .detail .head { display: flex; gap: .75rem; align-items: baseline; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .detail .name { font-size: 1.05rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: -.01em; }
  .detail .meta { font-size: .78rem; color: var(--ink-mute); }
  .detail p { margin: .5rem 0 0; font-size: .9rem; color: var(--ink-soft); line-height: 1.55; max-width: 78ch; }
  .detail p .k { color: var(--ink-mute); font-size: .76rem; letter-spacing: .1em; text-transform: uppercase; margin-right: .45rem; }
  .detail .proj { display: none; }
  .detail .proj.is-shown { display: block; }

  .derived { padding: 1rem 0 4rem; font-family: var(--font-primary); }
  .derived h2 {
    margin: 0 auto 1.25rem; padding-inline: 1.25rem;
    font-size: .78rem; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: .12em; text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--ink-mute);
  }
  .feature {
    width: 17rem; flex-shrink: 0;
    display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: .45rem;
    padding: 1.1rem 1.2rem; border-radius: var(--radius, 10px);
    border: 1px solid var(--rule-strong); background: var(--surface-raised);
  }
  .feature h3 { margin: 0; font-size: 1.05rem; letter-spacing: -.01em; color: var(--ink); }
  .feature p  { margin: 0; font-size: .88rem; line-height: 1.45; color: var(--ink-soft); }
  .feature code {
    margin-top: auto; align-self: flex-start;
    font-family: var(--font-mono, ui-monospace, Menlo, monospace); font-size: .75rem;
    color: var(--color-primary);
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .layer, .drift, .glow, .realms li { animation: none; }
  }
</style>
